<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · Arabia and the Gulf</p><h1 class="st-title">Alawi Sheikhdom</h1><p class="st-meta">1743 CE – 1967 CE (approx.) · capital Al Qasha</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">One of the smallest states of the Aden Protectorate, a tribal sheikhdom near the Yemeni frontier.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Alawi sheikhdom was a small tribal territory in the hills north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aden">Aden</a>, near <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/emirate-of-dhala">Dhala</a>, with its seat at Al Qasha. Like its neighbours, it gained independence in the 18th century as the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/qasimid-state">Qasimid State</a> withdrew from the south. Its early history is barely recorded.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The sheikhs ruled a few thousand people by tribal custom. The territory entered British protection through treaties in the late 19th century and was part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/aden-protectorate">Western Aden Protectorate</a>. In the 1960s it joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/federation-of-south-arabia">Federation of South Arabia</a>, the British-sponsored union of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> states.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/national-liberation-front-south-yemen">National Liberation Front</a> took power in 1967, the sheikhdom was abolished and absorbed into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/south-yemen">South Yemen</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/alawi-sheikhdom.jpg" alt="Alawi Sheikhdom" width="320" height="170"><figcaption>Image: Hamdan alyafei · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D8%B9%D9%84%D9%85_%D9%85%D8%B4%D9%8A%D8%AE%D8%A9_%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%B9%D9%84%D9%88%D9%8A.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1743 CE – 1967 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Al Qasha</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/yemen">Yemen</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Alawi, Sheikhdom of Alawi</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1855&amp;focus=alawi-sheikhdom" aria-label="Alawi Sheikhdom on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5904 1676 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Alawi Sheikhdom lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6224 1932L6295 1853M6224 1932L6313 1863M6224 1932L6236 1957"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6295 1853h0M6313 1863h0M6236 1957h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6224 1932h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6224 1932h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1855&amp;focus=alawi-sheikhdom">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
